---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import InstallCommand from '../components/InstallCommand.astro';
import {skills} from '../data/skills';
import {updateCommand,pluginMarketplaceCommand,pluginInstallCommand,pluginUpdateCommand} from '../data/install';
---
<Layout title="Install" active="install"><div class="document"><header class="doc-header"><p class="intro">Set up your toolkit</p><h1>Install the skills.</h1><p class="lede">Use the skills CLI for Claude Code or Codex, or install the managed Claude Code plugin.</p></header><section><h2>Install with the skills CLI</h2><p>Run the command in your project directory. You need Node.js 22.20.0 or newer, npm (which provides <code>npx</code>), Git, and network access. The interactive installer lets you choose skills, agents, and installation scope.</p><InstallCommand all chooseAgent/><p>The default is a project installation. Claude Code discovers project skills in <code>.claude/skills</code>; Codex uses <code>.agents/skills</code>. The installer offers symlink or copy installation. Choose global installation in the terminal, or add <code>--global</code>, when you want the skills across projects. Global agent directories are <code>~/.claude/skills</code> for Claude Code and <code>~/.codex/skills</code> for Codex.</p></section><section><h2>Install one skill</h2><p>Choose a skill and, optionally, your agent. Dependencies and backwards-compatible aliases are included when a skill needs them.</p><div class="skill-picker js-only"><label for="install-skill">Skill</label><select id="install-skill">{skills.map(s=><option value={s.slug}>{s.name}</option>)}</select></div>{skills.map((s,i)=><div class="individual-install" data-skill={s.slug} hidden={i!==0}><h3>{s.name}</h3><InstallCommand slug={s.slug} chooseAgent/><a href={`/skills/${s.slug}/`}>Read requirements and usage ↗</a></div>)}<noscript><p>Open a <a href="/">skill page</a> for its individual installation command.</p></noscript></section><section id="claude-plugin"><h2>Claude Code plugin</h2><p>The managed plugin packages the same skills for Claude Code. Register the MrCoder marketplace, then install the plugin. The marketplace is maintained by MrCoder.</p><div class="plugin-setup"><h3>1. Add the marketplace</h3><InstallCommand command={pluginMarketplaceCommand} label="Copy marketplace registration command"/><h3>2. Install the plugin</h3><InstallCommand command={pluginInstallCommand} label="Copy plugin installation command"/><p>Use the plugin namespace when invoking a skill, for example <code>/mrcoder-skills:diagram</code>. The plugin includes all eleven skills and the renhua alias.</p></div></section><section><h2>Ask your agent to use a skill</h2><p>Open your agent in the project and name the skill in your request:</p><pre class="example"><code>Use no-bs to explain this error in plain language.</code></pre><p>Each skill page has a specific example and requirements. Plugin skills use their documented plugin namespace. Skills guide the agent; they do not remove permission or review boundaries.</p></section><section><h2>Update your skills</h2><p>For skills CLI installations, run:</p><InstallCommand command={updateCommand}/><p>Keep your own changes separately before updating. For the Claude Code plugin, update its marketplace and plugin:</p><InstallCommand command={pluginUpdateCommand} label="Copy plugin update commands"/></section><section><h2>Package and platform notes</h2><ul><li><a href="/skills/search-conversation-history/">search-conversation-history</a> includes an executable, source, scripts, and reference files. Installing the package and building the local history index are separate steps. Follow its setup guide.</li><li><a href="/skills/overnight/">overnight</a> also needs unattended. The individual install command includes both packages.</li><li>The history package includes an Apple Silicon macOS binary. Other platforms need the documented source build.</li></ul><p>For manual installation, inspect the <a href="https://github.com/MrCoder/mrcoder.github.io/tree/master/skills">source packages</a> and copy the complete skill directory into your agent’s skills directory.</p></section><section><h2>Optional ZIP downloads</h2><p>Download the complete package and checksum before extracting:</p><ul><li><a href="/downloads/no-bs.zip">no-bs ZIP</a> · <a href="/downloads/no-bs.zip.sha256">SHA-256 checksum</a></li><li><a href="/downloads/search-conversation-history.zip">History ZIP</a> · <a href="/downloads/search-conversation-history.zip.sha256">SHA-256 checksum</a></li></ul><p>Run verification in the directory containing both downloaded files:</p><pre class="example"><code># macOS
shasum -a 256 -c search-conversation-history.zip.sha256
# Linux
sha256sum -c search-conversation-history.zip.sha256</code></pre><p>Only extract after verification passes. For manual updates, use a fresh directory before replacing the installed package; extracting over it can leave removed files behind.</p></section></div></Layout>
<script>const picker=document.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('#install-skill');picker?.addEventListener('change',()=>document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.individual-install').forEach(el=>el.hidden=el.dataset.skill!==picker.value));</script>
